<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Madrid (1750)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1750</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Madrid of 1750 between Portugal and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> replaced the line of the Treaty of Tordesillas with borders in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a> based on actual occupation. Portugal secured most of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amazon">Amazon</a> basin and the interior of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, giving up Colonia do Sacramento in exchange for the Seven Missions east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruguay">Uruguay</a> River. Joint commissions were sent to map the frontiers, and the treaty was annulled in 1761.</p></div>
